# IMPORTANT: this file must live at the WORKSPACE ROOT, not inside
# firmware/. esp-idf-sys's build script (build/native/cargo_driver.rs in
# esp-idf-sys 0.36.1) resolves the default "sdkconfig.defaults" filename
# via `.abspath_relative_to(&workspace_dir)`, i.e. relative to the Cargo
# workspace root -- NOT the firmware crate directory -- and there is no
# `[package.metadata.esp-idf-sys]` override in this workspace to change
# that. This file used to live at firmware/sdkconfig.defaults (from
# before the core/firmware/emulator workspace split) and was SILENTLY
# NEVER READ as a result: confirmed while investigating bead
# ai-bitwarden-hw-key-1k8's stack overflow, the generated sdkconfig
# showed the raw ESP-IDF default (3584) even though this file already
# said 8000. Moved here as part of that fix -- if this file appears to
# have no effect again, check it's still at the workspace root, not a
# crate subdirectory.
#
# Rust often needs a bit of an extra main task stack size compared to C (the default is 3K)
# Bumped 8000 -> 32768 (bead ai-bitwarden-hw-key-1k8): opening the credential
# detail view (Activate on the list) overflowed the 8000-byte stack on real
# hardware ("A stack overflow in task main has been detected"). Investigated
# core/src/credential_detail_view.rs and core/src/render/secret_field.rs for
# an accidental large stack allocation (a framebuffer-sized local, a big
# fixed array, a big struct by value) -- none found; FrameBuffer565 is
# Vec-backed (heap), FontRenderer is a thin static-table wrapper (per its
# own doc comment), and the only fixed-size stack arrays anywhere in the
# render core are 4-byte UTF-8 scratch buffers shared with the list view
# (which does NOT overflow). The real, structural difference: the detail
# view's render_fields()/render_field() call u8g2_fonts's
# get_rendered_dimensions_aligned (font metric measurement) TWICE per
# field per render (line_height() for both the label and value font, via
# field_height()) in addition to the actual draw call, and nest
# DrawTargetExt::clipped() two levels deep (render_fields -> render_field
# -> SecretField::render for the password field) -- versus the list
# view's flat per-row draw using precomputed constants
# (NAME_LINE_FOOTPRINT/USERNAME_LINE_FOOTPRINT in render/list.rs), with no
# runtime font-metric queries at all. In an unoptimized debug build that's
# genuinely deeper, more-repeated generic/monomorphized call-graph depth
# per render, not a leak -- a legitimate stack-budget shortfall, not an
# accidental allocation bug. 32768 is generous headroom (this board has
# hundreds of KB of SRAM free per the boot heap_init log), not a tightly
# tuned minimum -- deliberately so a future detail-view feature (more
# fields, deeper nesting) doesn't reopen this exact bug at a slightly
# higher threshold.
CONFIG_ESP_MAIN_TASK_STACK_SIZE=32768

# Use this to set FreeRTOS kernel tick frequency to 1000 Hz (100 Hz by default).
# This allows to use 1 ms granuality for thread sleeps (10 ms by default).
#CONFIG_FREERTOS_HZ=1000

# Workaround for https://github.com/espressif/esp-idf/issues/7631
#CONFIG_MBEDTLS_CERTIFICATE_BUNDLE=n
#CONFIG_MBEDTLS_CERTIFICATE_BUNDLE_DEFAULT_FULL=n
